  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Opened on 1 July 2026 and inaugurated on 30 July by the mayor, the Pipady dog beach is Toulon's second swimming area dedicated to dogs, after the Tabarly cove, set up on an inlet to the right of the Tour Royale. The 2,000 sqm space is fully fenced, letting dogs roam completely freely, separated from the site's other users (toulon.fr).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The city publishes neither hours nor fees for this area. Two-way signage organises circulation: swimmers and visitors are asked to head left, while dogs have their own lane to the right. The mayor announced a water point "soon" (30 July 2026) and reminds owners that they must pick up droppings.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a dog owner interviewed at the inauguration finds the spot shaded in the morning (RCF Méditerranée, 30 July 2026) — remember to bring water until the announced water point is installed.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Tour Royale, a cannon fort built in 1514 on the initiative of Louis XII and listed as a historic monument, overlooks the beach. Toulon's other dog beach, the <a href="/en/fiche-anse-tabarly-toulon">Tabarly cove</a>, is in the Mourillon area and is eventually to close in favour of Pipady.</p>
    </div>

